  "sarneg_guideTitle": "SARNEG or real encryption?",
  "sarneg_guideBody": "SARNEG swaps digits for letters with one shared word. Anyone who hears a few messages can work the word out, so it only keeps numbers from a casual listener. It is not encryption.\n\nFor real secrecy, use a private channel with its own key. The radio encrypts everything on it, and only people with the key can read it.\n\nSARNEG still helps on top of that: on shared or public channels, through relays and bridges, in logs and screenshots, and against someone who has the channel key but not the code word.",
